            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The playbook keys configured under "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "network"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " control the network requests initiated by Antora. These requests, at present, include those made by the git client in the content aggregator and the HTTP client in the UI loader."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In most cases, users will choose to use the environment variables mapped to the keys in this category ("
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "http_proxy"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "https_proxy"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "no_proxy"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " ) instead of defining them in the playbook. However, being able to set them in the playbook or via the mapped CLI option does offer the possibility of controlling these settings per Antora run. Recall that environment variables take precedence over keys defined in the playbook file, but get overridden by the CLI option for that same key."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "note"
          }
